      "problem": "Find the points of intersection of the parabola $(y-2)^2=4(x+1)$ with the $y$-axis.",
      "worked_solution": "To find the points of intersection of the parabola with the $y$-axis, we set $x=0$ and solve the resulting equation for $y\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-2)^{2} & =4(x+1) \\\\ (y-2)^{2} & =4(0+1) \\\\ (y-2)^{2} & =4 \\\\ y-2 & =\\pm 2 \\\\ y & =2\\pm 2 \\\\ y & =0,4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parabola intersects the $y$-axis $(0,0)$ and $(0,4).$",
